<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Samoa</h1><p class="st-meta">1873 CE – 1899 CE (approx.) · capital Mulinuʻu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Samoan national government contested by rival chiefly lines and by Germany, Britain and the United States, which ended in the islands' partition in 1899.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samoan-islands">Samoa</a> was divided among districts and great titles such as Malietoa, Tupua <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupua-tamasese-titimaea">Tamasese</a> and Mataʻafa. As the German firm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/j-c-godeffroy-and-sohn">Godeffroy</a> developed plantations near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apia">Apia</a>, Samoan chiefs formed a central government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mulinuu">Mulinuʻu</a> in 1873, with a council of chiefs and an assembly. The American adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-steinberger">Albert Steinberger</a> acted as premier until British and American consuls had him deported in 1876.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kingship, held mostly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malietoa-laupepa">Malietoa Laupepa</a>, was repeatedly disputed in civil wars, with each rival courting a foreign power. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupua-tamasese-titimaea">Tamasese</a> against Laupepa in 1887, and a naval confrontation at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apia">Apia</a> ended only when a hurricane wrecked the German and American warships in 1889. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-berlin-1889">Berlin Treaty</a> of 1889 restored Laupepa under a three-power supervision. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-louis-stevenson">Robert Louis Stevenson</a>, living at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vailima">Vailima</a>, wrote against foreign meddling.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malietoa-laupepa">Laupepa</a>'s death in 1898, war between supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mataafa-iosefo">Mataʻafa Iosefo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malietoa-tanumafili-i">Malietoa Tanumafili I</a> drew in foreign navies. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899">Tripartite Convention of 1899</a> abolished the kingship and partitioned the islands into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-samoa">German Samoa</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/american-samoa">American Samoa</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-samoa.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Samoa" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Malietoa Laupepa Vector: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Samoa_(1873%E2%80%931886,_1889%E2%80%931900).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1873 CE – 1899 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mulinuʻu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Malietoa Laupepa, Mataʻafa Iosefo, Malietoa Tanumafili I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Samoan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/samoa">Samoa</a>, <a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Samoan Kingdom, Malietoa kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1886&amp;focus=kingdom-of-samoa" aria-label="Kingdom of Samoa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="-26 2692 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Samoa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M294 2948L5300 622M294 2948L4997 651M294 2948L2570 1008M294 2948L293 2949M294 2948L328 2965"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5300 622h0M4997 651h0M2570 1008h0M293 2949h0M328 2965h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M294 2948h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M294 2948h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mulinuʻu. <a href="/atlas?year=1886&amp;focus=kingdom-of-samoa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
